# Citation metadata in the Citation File Format (CFF), which GitHub shows under "Cite
# this repository" and Zenodo reads when a release is archived. Keep `version` in
# step with the version in the Snakefile and the README banner, and add the release
# date at release time:
#     date-released: YYYY-MM-DD
# The DOI below is the Zenodo concept DOI, which always resolves to the newest
# release; each release also has a DOI of its own, listed on Zenodo and in
# docs/about/citation.md.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MetaFlux in your work, please cite it as below, and cite the tools and reference databases it runs (see the citation page of the documentation)."
type: software
title: "MetaFlux: a unified short-read multi-marker amplicon and shotgun taxonomic profiling workflow"
version: 2.5.0
authors:
  - family-names: Antonielli
    given-names: Livio
    affiliation: AIT Austrian Institute of Technology
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/iLivius/MetaFlux
url: https://iLivius.github.io/MetaFlux/
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22876451
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22876451
    description: Zenodo concept DOI, resolving to the newest release
abstract: >-
  A Snakemake workflow that takes raw paired-end short reads to a taxonomically
  annotated abundance table in one of two modes: amplicon (DADA2-based, for the 16S
  rRNA, ITS, 18S rRNA, gyrB and rpoB markers, with an optional 16S phylogeny) and
  shotgun (Kraken2 + Bracken, or sylph). Both modes run from one command and one
  config file and end in one MultiQC report.
keywords:
  - metagenomics
  - amplicon sequencing
  - 16S rRNA
  - ITS
  - 18S rRNA
  - gyrB
  - rpoB
  - DADA2
  - Snakemake
  - taxonomic profiling
  - shotgun metagenomics
  - Kraken2
  - sylph
  - phylogenetics
  - bioinformatics workflow
  - reproducibility
